1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,800
In 2012, NASA's fire record jumps tenfold.

2
00:00:04,050 --> 00:00:06,100
The fires didn't change.
The satellite did.

3
00:00:06,350 --> 00:00:09,850
So we built a model that learns how
both satellites see, area by area.

4
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:14,250
On unseen years, error drops
from 77 to 14%,

5
00:00:14,350 --> 00:00:16,400
and every value shows its margin.

6
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:19,000
Draw any area:
Zij fits it live,

7
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:21,600
and tells responders
if this season's normal.

8
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:23,500
And it reveals what the split record hid:

9
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,600
in the Delta, detected burning
rose after the 2004 ban,

10
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:28,850
and has halved since 2018.
